{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronTwoBodyKernel","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerFactorial"],"declarations":38,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.crossTerm_parity_ratio_cap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.crossTerm_parity_ratio_cap","kind":"theorem","line":485,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L485-L490","doc":"The same cap transfers to the `n = 4` interleaved cross term, by §7. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_parity_ratio_cap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_parity_ratio_cap","kind":"theorem","line":467,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L467-L483","doc":"**THE CAP.**  On the physical range `|T_z| ≤ 1` the `n = 4` parity ratio\ncannot exceed `(q⁴−1)/(q⁴+1)` in magnitude, for any bond assignment.\n\nThis is the scope-(b) content of the second tranche: it is not that the observed\nratio is missed by some amount, it is that the interleaved `n = 4` cross term has\nno assignment reaching past this bound at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.parityRatioSlope_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.parityRatioSlope_pos","kind":"theorem","line":461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L461-L465","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.parityRatioSlope_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.parityRatioSlope_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":456,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L456-L459","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.one_le_pow_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.one_le_pow_four","kind":"theorem","line":451,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L451-L454","doc":"`1 ≤ q` forces `1 ≤ q⁴` — the step both bounds below need. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.parityRatioSlope_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.parityRatioSlope_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":444,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L444-L449","doc":"The slope is strictly positive for `q > 1`, and strictly below `1` for every\n`q` — so the ratio is bounded by `1` in magnitude on `|T_z| ≤ 1`, whatever `q` is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_parity_ratio_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_parity_ratio_eq","kind":"theorem","line":413,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L413-L442","doc":"**The parity ratio is exactly `slope · T_z`.**\n\nBoth parts were computed in §2: the odd part is `(h/2)·T_z` and the even part is\nthe constant `z_D − h/2 = (q⁴+1)/(2q(q²+1))`.  Their quotient collapses to\n`(q⁴−1)/(q⁴+1)` times `T_z`, with the `2q(q²+1)` cancelling against `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.parityRatioSlope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.parityRatioSlope","kind":"def","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L410-L411","doc":"The exact parity-ratio slope of the bond channel: `(q⁴ − 1)/(q⁴ + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.crossTerm_oddPart_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.crossTerm_oddPart_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":367,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L367-L381","doc":"**The transfer, stated as the prune it is.**  At every `q > 1` the interleaved\ncross term has a nonzero `T_z`-odd part, with the *same* odd/even ratio as the bond\nfactor it multiplies.  The word-class route can supply magnitude; it cannot supply a\ndifferent charge structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.markovDefect_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.markovDefect_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L352-L365","doc":"The defect does not vanish at any `q > 1`: `z² − hz − 1 = −(q⁴+q²+1)/(q²+1)²`,\nwhich is strictly negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.crossTerm_even_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.crossTerm_even_iff","kind":"theorem","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L337-L350","doc":"**The cross term is even in `T_z` iff the bond factor is** (given a nonvanishing\ndefect) — so §3's exclusion transfers: at every `q > 1` the cross term is odd too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.crossTerm_parity_ratio_eq_bond","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.crossTerm_parity_ratio_eq_bond","kind":"theorem","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L325-L335","doc":"**The cross term's parity ratio is the bond factor's own.**\n\nSo the interleaved word class changes the *magnitude* of the bond channel — which is\nwhat `qou-kru4` wants it for, the defect being negative and hence extra binding — and\nprovably does **not** change its charge parity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.crossTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.crossTerm","kind":"def","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L321-L323","doc":"The `n = 4` interleaved cross term, as a function of the peeled bond's isospin\nprojection: `Δ(T_z) = f(T_z) · (z² − hz − 1)`, the identity measured above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.markovDefect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.markovDefect","kind":"def","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L317-L319","doc":"The convention-D Markov defect `z² − hz − 1`.  It is a function of `q` alone, so\nit is charge-blind by construction — that is the whole reason §7 applies to it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.parity_ratio_const_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.parity_ratio_const_mul","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L307-L315","doc":"**A charge-blind multiplier leaves the parity ratio exactly fixed.**\n\n`c` is any nonzero scalar not depending on `T_z`.  Both parts scale by `c`, so the\nratio does not move at all — no choice of `c`, however large, however `q`-dependent,\nchanges it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.oddPart_const_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.oddPart_const_mul","kind":"theorem","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L303-L305","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.evenPart_const_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.evenPart_const_mul","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L299-L301","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.oddPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.oddPart","kind":"def","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L296-L297","doc":"Mirror-odd part of a function of the pair isospin projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.evenPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.evenPart","kind":"def","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L293-L294","doc":"Mirror-even part of a function of the pair isospin projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.channels_opposite_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.channels_opposite_parity","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L233-L246","doc":"**The two channels carry opposite `T_z` parity.**\n\nAt every `q > 1`: the bond channel has a nonzero `T_z`-odd part, and the\nmultiplet channel has none.  So within this framework the charge-symmetry\nviolation is located entirely in the bond layer, it is exactly the Hecke\ndeformation, and it cannot be tuned away by any choice of `q`.\n\nRead as guidance rather than as a result: a charge-symmetric strong channel has\nto come from somewhere other than an interface factor affine in the neutron\ncount, and the multiplet weight is the corpus's standing candidate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.multipletWeight_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.multipletWeight_even","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L221-L229","doc":"**The multiplet weight is even in `T_z`, for every `q`.**\n\nTrivially so — it reads only `|T_z|`.  That triviality is the finding: evenness\ncosts the multiplet channel nothing, while the bond channel cannot have it at any\n`q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.multipletWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.multipletWeight","kind":"def","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L213-L219","doc":"The two-row isospin multiplet weight `[2T+1]_q` at `T = |T_z|`.\n\nTwo-row partitions `λ = (a,b) ⊢ A` are the isospin multiplets, with\n`T = (a−b)/2` and `|N − Z| = a − b = 2T` (bean `qou-xwur`); the Wenzl weight of\nthe multiplet is the quantum dimension `[2T+1]_q`.  Indexed by the integer\nprojection here, since that is what a parity statement needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondL_pp_ne_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondL_pp_ne_nn","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L198-L209","doc":"**The p–p and n–n bond energies differ**, for every `q` whose deformation\nlies in `(0,1)` — which includes the substrate, where `h(q₀) ≈ 0.209`.\n\nThis is the energy-level form of §3 and is a one-line consequence of\n`bondL_strictMono`, already proved in the imported file: the bond energy is\nstrictly increasing in the colour weight, and p–p sits at `t = 0` while n–n sits\nat `t = 1`.  Charge symmetry demands these be equal; strict monotonicity forbids\nit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.writheExponent_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.writheExponent_odd","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L194-L196","doc":"The writhe exponent is purely `T_z`-odd:  `t(T_z) − ½ = −T_z/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_oddPart_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_oddPart_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L180-L186","doc":"**Restated as the exclusion it is: at every `q > 1` the bond channel has a\nnonzero `T_z`-odd part.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.hq_pos_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.hq_pos_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L171-L178","doc":"`1 < q` forces a strictly positive Hecke deformation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_even_iff_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_even_iff_classical","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L161-L169","doc":"**The bond layer is charge-symmetric only in the classical limit.**\n\nFor every `q > 0`, the interface family is even in `T_z` iff `q = 1`.  So at any\ngenuine deformation — the substrate sits at `q₀ ≈ 1.10998` — the bond channel\ncarries a nonzero `T_z`-odd part, and it is the deformation itself that breaks\ncharge symmetry.  No choice of `q > 1` avoids this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.hq_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.hq_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L151-L159","doc":"`h(q) = q − q⁻¹` vanishes exactly at `q = 1`, among positive `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_even_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_even_iff","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L136-L149","doc":"**The bond factor is even in `T_z` iff the Hecke deformation vanishes.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_pp_sub_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_pp_sub_nn","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L129-L132","doc":"The p–p / n–n gap is exactly `h(q)`, for every `q`.  (Measured numerically at\nthe proton pin as `|f_pp − f_nn| = h = 0.20906029879563931543`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_oddPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_oddPart","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L122-L127","doc":"**The `T_z`-odd part is exactly `(h/2)·T_z`.**  This is the whole content of\nthe file: the charge-symmetry violation of the bond layer *is* the Hecke\ndeformation parameter, with no other source and no other size. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_evenPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_evenPart","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L117-L120","doc":"The `T_z`-**even** part is constant: it does not see `T_z` at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz_eq","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L110-L115","doc":"**The bond factor is affine in `T_z`**, with intercept `z_D − h/2` and slope\n`h/2`:  `f(T_z) = (z_D − h/2) + (h/2)·T_z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.bondOfTz","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L105-L106","doc":"The bond factor read as a function of the pair isospin projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.weightOfTz_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.weightOfTz_zero","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L102-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.weightOfTz_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.weightOfTz_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L99-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.weightOfTz_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.weightOfTz_one","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L97-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.weightOfTz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondChannelTzParity.weightOfTz","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondChannelTzParity.lean#L90-L95","doc":"The `σ⁻¹`-branch weight of a pair with isospin projection `T_z`:\n`t(T_z) = (1 − T_z)/2`.\n\n`T_z = +1` (p–p) ↦ `t = 0`; `T_z = 0` (p–n) ↦ `t = ½`; `T_z = −1` (n–n) ↦ `t = 1`,\nmatching `interfaceFactor`'s own reading of its second argument. ","signatureChunk":0}]}